# Recipes, the pantry, the recipe book and experiments (recipes.ron, design/handson.md §4).
# .lore = Lida's handwritten line in the book (amber italics). .teach = the bubble when someone shows you.
# English placeholder texts in every language until T9 (see handson_TODO.txt).

# --- recipes: starters ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
recipe.r_black.name
* Black, like Lida made it

recipe.r_black.desc
* A slow pour-over, nothing added. Honest coffee for honest hours.

recipe.r_black.lore
* Pour slowly. Nobody who comes at night is in a hurry, even when they say they are.

recipe.r_cappuccino.name
* Cappuccino

recipe.r_cappuccino.desc
* Espresso under a soft cap of milk foam.

recipe.r_cappuccino.lore
* Milk sings when it's ready. Listen, don't look.

recipe.r_lemon_tea.name
* Tea with lemon

recipe.r_lemon_tea.desc
* Black tea, a slice of lemon, steeped just long enough.

recipe.r_lemon_tea.lore
* Lift the bag before it turns bitter. People are the same.

recipe.r_topinka.name
* Topinka

recipe.r_topinka.desc
* Fried bread rubbed with garlic, the taxi-rank breakfast.

recipe.r_topinka.lore
* Two rubs of garlic for drivers, three for anyone who looks sad.

recipe.r_garlic_soup.name
* Česnečka

recipe.r_garlic_soup.desc
* Garlic soup with potato and croutons. It fixes most things.

recipe.r_garlic_soup.lore
* Česnečka cures colds, hangovers and small heartbreaks. Big ones need kulajda.

recipe.r_chlebicek.name
* Chlebíček

recipe.r_chlebicek.desc
* An open sandwich with potato salad, ham and a slice of egg.

recipe.r_chlebicek.lore
* Make it pretty. A chlebíček is a small party on a plate.

# --- recipes: grandma's cards ------------------------------------------------------------------------
recipe.r_kolac.name
* Koláč

recipe.r_kolac.desc
* A round little cake with tvaroh and plum jam.

recipe.r_kolac.lore
* Jam in the middle, crumble on top, and always one more than you think you'll need.

recipe.r_oat_flat_white.name
* Oat flat white

recipe.r_oat_flat_white.desc
* Velvety oat milk over a double espresso, with a little art on top.

recipe.r_oat_flat_white.lore
* The young ones like it with oats. Fine. Draw them a heart and they'll come back.

recipe.r_medovnik.name
* Medovník

recipe.r_medovnik.desc
* Layered honey cake with cream, served cold.

recipe.r_medovnik.lore
* Honey cake needs a night to rest. So do we.

recipe.r_chai.name
* Chai

recipe.r_chai.desc
* Black tea with warm milk and spice.

recipe.r_chai.lore
* Cinnamon and clove, a pinch of each, and milk only when the tea is dark.

recipe.r_hot_chocolate.name
* Hot chocolate

recipe.r_hot_chocolate.desc
* Thick cocoa with steamed milk.

recipe.r_hot_chocolate.lore
* For anyone who's cold, or eight, or both.

recipe.r_varenyky.name
* Varenyky with potato & mushroom

recipe.r_varenyky.desc
* Dumplings with potato and mushroom, smetana and crispy onion.

recipe.r_varenyky.lore
* A traveller from Lviv taught me these, one snowy night. Pinch the edges like you mean it.

recipe.r_pirohy.name
* Bryndzové pirohy

recipe.r_pirohy.desc
* Potato pockets with sheep's cheese and a little bacon.

recipe.r_pirohy.lore
* For the Slovak drivers. They stop missing home for exactly one plate.

recipe.r_night_train.name
* Night Train

recipe.r_night_train.desc
* A strong pour-over with cocoa and spice — the café's own.

recipe.r_night_train.lore
* Strong enough for the last train, soft enough for the first one.

recipe.r_svarak.name
* Svařák

recipe.r_svarak.desc
* Mulled red wine with spice and a little sugar. Never boiled.

recipe.r_svarak.lore
* Warm it, never boil it. Wine that boils has given up.

# --- recipes: story and the people who teach ---------------------------------------------------------
recipe.r_kulajda.name
* Grandma's kulajda

recipe.r_kulajda.desc
* Creamy mushroom and dill soup with potato — Lida's own.

recipe.r_kulajda.lore
* Dill at the very end. And don't tell Vera how much cream.

recipe.r_turek.name
* Turek, taxi-rank style

recipe.r_turek.desc
* Coffee boiled in the cup with sugar, grounds left to settle.

recipe.r_turek.lore
* Mirek's. Let it settle. He always did.

recipe.r_turek.teach
* Stir three times, then hands off. Let the grounds sit down, like a tired driver.

recipe.r_vera_kolac.name
* Vera's poppy-seed koláč, warmed

recipe.r_vera_kolac.desc
* Poppy seed and tvaroh, warmed through, the way Vera insists.

recipe.r_vera_kolac.lore
* Vera's is better. Never tell her I wrote that.

recipe.r_vera_kolac.teach
* Warm it, child. A cold koláč is a sad koláč. Poppy seed first, then the tvaroh.

recipe.r_rn333_tea.name
* Tea, two sugars

recipe.r_rn333_tea.desc
* Black tea with lemon and exactly two sugars.

recipe.r_rn333_tea.lore
* Two sugars. He always took two.

recipe.r_lori_encore.name
* Lori's encore

recipe.r_lori_encore.desc
* Hot chocolate with a pinch of chili.

recipe.r_lori_encore.lore
* A pinch of fire for the singer. Not a spoon. A pinch.

recipe.r_lori_encore.teach
* Just a pinch of chili, love. It warms the voice from the inside.

recipe.r_linden_tea.name
* Linden tea with honey

recipe.r_linden_tea.desc
* Lime-blossom tea, golden and gentle, with honey.

recipe.r_linden_tea.lore
* Linden for sleep and for singers. Honey, always honey.

recipe.r_moon_latte.name
* Moonlight latte

recipe.r_moon_latte.desc
* Oat milk turned dusk-blue with butterfly pea, a crescent on top.

recipe.r_moon_latte.lore
* Not mine, this one. Yours. Write it down so someone finds it one day.

# --- SHOULD: the crew's recipes --------------------------------------------------------------------------
recipe.r_raf.name
* Raf coffee (Kyiv-style)

recipe.r_raf.desc
* Espresso whisked with cream and vanilla into something like a cloud.

recipe.r_raf.lore
* Oleh's. Sweet, soft, and a little homesick.

recipe.r_raf.teach
* In Kyiv we steam the coffee with the cream. Watch for the vanilla drop — there!

recipe.r_borscht.name
* Borscht with smetana

recipe.r_borscht.desc
* Beetroot soup, deep ruby, with a spoon of smetana.

recipe.r_borscht.lore
* The colour is the whole secret. Beetroot in on time, or it goes brown and sulks.

recipe.r_borscht.teach
* My mother's borscht. Beetroot goes in at the right moment — I'll tell you when.

recipe.r_buchty.name
* Kuba's buchty with povidla

recipe.r_buchty.desc
* Soft baked buns filled with plum povidla, sugar on top.

recipe.r_buchty.lore
* The boy has been baking secretly. Let him think nobody noticed.

recipe.r_buchty.teach
* Mr Holub showed me. Don't tell him I'm showing you — he'll get all proud.

recipe.r_tatra_tea.name
* Tatra herb tea

recipe.r_tatra_tea.desc
* Mountain herbs, honey and lemon, like a hut in the Tatras.

recipe.r_tatra_tea.lore
* Natália's. It smells like a mountain after rain.

recipe.r_tatra_tea.teach
* My granny picked these above Ždiar. Honey first, lemon at the end.

recipe.r_espresso_tonic.name
* Platform espresso tonic

recipe.r_espresso_tonic.desc
* Espresso poured slowly over tonic and ice. Bitter, bright, cold.

recipe.r_espresso_tonic.lore
* Filip calls it exam fuel. I call it a cold drink with opinions.

recipe.r_espresso_tonic.teach
* Pour it slowly over the ice, or it fizzes everywhere. Trust me. I've been there.

recipe.r_uzvar.name
* Uzvar

recipe.r_uzvar.desc
* A warm drink of dried fruit and honey, like Christmas in Lviv.

recipe.r_uzvar.lore
* From the parcel. Dried pears and plums and someone's love, all in one pot.

